193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (ZIMRA's website is not struggling for relevance or use  it is struggling to keep its technical foundation in step with how much taxpayers now depend on it.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (The traffic and ranking data make the strongest case for the site's current trajectory. A 51% jump in monthly visits, an improving bounce rate, and a self-service portal that now accounts for the large majority of all site activity all point to a platform taxpayers are actively using to get things done, not merely browsing. The #1 ranking secured for ZIMRA's TaRMS login query reinforces this: a narrow technical win with an outsized real-world benefit, since it helps route taxpayers to the legitimate portal rather than a lookalike.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (Set against that success, the technical and backlink findings are more than routine SEO housekeeping. The 142 broken scripts, the missing sitemap, and the duplicate-content issues are concentrated around the same portal that carries most of ZIMRA's traffic, which raises their stakes well above what identical issues would mean on an ordinary commercial site. The backlink audit adds a further dimension: a cluster of over 250 links carrying black-hat spam anchor text is not just a ranking-dilution concern but a pattern worth ZIMRA's security team treating seriously, given how frequently tax authorities are targeted for impersonation.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (None of this points to a site in crisis. It points to a site whose growth has outpaced its maintenance cycle ,a common and correctable position, provided the fixes are sequenced correctly. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
